Delete EC2 Instance Using Terraform
Task Overview
Temporarily clean up an unused AWS EC2 instance named devops-ec2 in the us-east-1 region using Terraform while ensuring the provisioning code remains intact for future use.

Step-by-Step Instructions
Step 1: Open the Terminal
Open the integrated terminal in your VS Code environment on the iac-server node.

Step 2: Navigate to the Terraform Working Directory
Go to the directory where your configuration files (main.tf, provider.tf, etc.) are located:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
Step 3: Target and Destroy the EC2 Instance
Run the destroy command targeting the specific EC2 resource (aws_instance.ec2) to terminate the instance without deleting your configuration files:

Bash
terraform destroy -target=aws_instance.ec2
Example Terminal Output:
Plaintext
aws_instance.ec2: Refreshing state... [id=i-a397bc881c6044f95]

Terraform used the selected providers to generate the
following execution plan. Resource actions are indicated with
the following symbols:
  - destroy

Terraform will perform the following actions:

  # aws_instance.ec2 will be destroyed
  - resource "aws_instance" "ec2" {
      ...
      - id                                   = "i-a397bc881c6044f95" -> null
      - instance_state                       = "running" -> null
      - instance_type                        = "t2.micro" -> null
      - tags                                 = {
          - "Name" = "devops-ec2"
        } -> null
      ...
    }

Plan: 0 to add, 0 to change, 1 to destroy.
Step 4: Confirm the Destruction
When prompted by Terraform to confirm, type:

Plaintext
yes
Example Completion Output:
Plaintext
aws_instance.ec2: Destroying... [id=i-a397bc881c6044f95]
aws_instance.ec2: Still destroying... [id=i-a397bc881c6044f95, 10s elapsed]
aws_instance.ec2: Destruction complete after 10s

Destroy complete! Resources: 1 destroyed.
Step 5: Verify Instance State
To ensure the instance has been completely terminated and the state is clean, verify that no pending resources remain:

Bash
terraform plan
